  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a 5% thermal-testing benchmark but do not bar sales above it, instead requiring regulator review and corrective action; per-model results go to owners and regulators but not the public. Remote shut-off retrofit is set at six years, fire suppression at 36 months, and a mandatory model-specific recall triggers at 8 incidents per 100,000 with no phase-in. Reporting is limited to serious incidents within 24 hours, with customer notice within 72 hours, and minor incidents are not individually reportable."
